Naming note: internal identifiers (element ids/classes, localStorage keys
"paios-*", "X-PAIOS-*" HTTP headers, "PAIOS_*" environment variables, Python
module names, and script paths such as scripts/paios-*) intentionally retain
the historical "paios" spelling so existing installs keep working. They refer
to this project, MyPaiOS.

Third-party code adapted into this repository
---------------------------------------------
Portions of MyPaiOS were adapted from the following open-source projects.
Original authors retain copyright over the adapted portions. Full license
texts are kept in the licenses/ directory; details and file locations are in
ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md. Every adaptation below was made UPSTREAM IN ODYSSEUS,
before the MyPaiOS fork point; MyPaiOS inherited them and expanded their
attribution.

- opencode — https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
  (originally opencode-ai/opencode) — MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 opencode.
  Upstream Odysseus declared this project "adapted for agent-loop /
  tool-execution patterns and UI concepts"; that declaration is preserved.
  Specifically identified: the GitHub Copilot provider logic (src/copilot.py)
  is a Python port of opencode's Copilot implementation.

- llmfit by Alex Jones — https://github.com/AlexsJones/llmfit — MIT License.
  Hardware detection, quant-aware model-fit scoring, and the model catalog
  behind the Cookbook feature (services/hwfit/).

- Tongyi DeepResearch by Alibaba-NLP / Tongyi Lab —
  https://github.com/Alibaba-NLP/DeepResearch — Apache License 2.0.
  Upstream Odysseus declared this project adapted for its Deep Research
  feature (services/research/, src/research_handler.py,
  routes/research_routes.py, services/search/); that declaration is preserved.
  Specifically identified: the goal-based content-extraction prompt
  (src/goal_based_extractor.py) is taken near-verbatim from DeepResearch's
  inference/prompt.py. Modified files carry change notices per Apache-2.0
  §4(b).

- talon by Mailgun Technologies, Inc. — https://github.com/mailgun/talon —
  Apache License 2.0. The multilingual email quote-detection patterns in
  static/js/emailLibrary/utils.js are adapted from talon's quotation-parsing
